    "cmake/OpenMXCPU.cmake"
  ],
  "findings": [
    "Existing CPU references already use OpenMP ELPA and measured three-thread OpenMP BLIS with validated disjoint three-core rank binding.",
    "The current optimization changes GPU scheduling, HIP construction/density kernels and GPU solver completion; elpa2 does not select those branches.",
    "The gpusolver2 ELPA teardown correction affects GPU bridge handles, not ordinary elpa2 CPU solves; the caller thread limit is restored.",
    "The CPU-only configure probe correction unsets an Intel MPI PMI variable on Slurm systems; it does not disable or rebuild the already validated Open MPI ELPA installation on Sirius.",
    "Core and host SIMD library hashes exactly match the previous fork CPU build.",
    "The noncollinear band common path now includes one MPI_Allreduce per SCF step for the MI300A branch decision, plus small state bookkeeping. This small dispatch overhead is acknowledged; no zero CPU effect or byte-identical executable claim is made."
  ],
  "limitation": "CPU timings remain historical single measurements with the older CPU executable, not fresh timings of the current GPU binary with OPENMX_GPU=0. L2/L3 have no completed CPU suite and would need new CPU measurements for speedups or matched Sirius CPU numerical comparisons.",
